# Fixtures for `tools/watchdog --dry-run` (ticket #91). Sourced by tools/watchdog, so `$R` is the
# repo root and `$HOME` is real: one file per thing a check reads, so all five cases run offline.
# The session files are trimmed pi session jsonl (real shape, stub content): the lead's is the
# newest and ends in a compaction (case 3), the driver's is idle 70 min (case 4). The driver runs
# pi in tools/sandbox with --cwd $R, so its session dir is named after $R (factory/driver.md).
# The process table: the forwarders (case 5) run in it. The leads (t1nm, pirust-driver) are NOT
# running in this fixture, so cases 1, 2 and 5 all fire (cases 3, 4 are gated by them running;
# run with PIRUST_LS_JSON=watchdog-ls-healthy.json to see those, and with no action to see 1, 2, 5).
# The state and digest writes go to a throwaway dir in --dry-run, so these fixtures are read-only.
PIRUST_SESSIONS="$R/test/fixtures/watchdog-sessions/--home-zerodawn-private-pirust--"
PIRUST_DRIVER_SESS_DIR="$R/test/fixtures/watchdog-sessions/--home-zerodawn-private-pirust-wt-91--"
PIRUST_DIGEST="${PIRUST_DIGEST:-$R/test/fixtures/watchdog-digest.log}"
PIRUST_PROCS="${PIRUST_PROCS:-$R/test/fixtures/watchdog-procs.txt}"
PIRUST_LS_JSON="${PIRUST_LS_JSON:-$R/test/fixtures/watchdog-ls-gone.json}"
PIRUST_STATE="${PIRUST_STATE:-$R/test/fixtures/watchdog-state}"
PIRUST_DRIVER_SESSION="$R/test/fixtures/watchdog-sessions/--home-zerodawn-private-pirust-wt-91--/2026-11-16T21-50-00-000Z_01a1e689-0000-7000-8000-000000000002.jsonl"
PIRUST_LEAD_MODEL=anthropic/claude-opus-5.5
